# GRANTS: kiosk-1's answer to ../RUNNABLES. What this crew wears, on purpose.
#
# DRAFT, 2026-09-26. The runner paths are unconfirmed until the media node says
# how it actually starts its tools; see `runner` below.
#
# This is the crew's half. RUNNABLES says what each verb claims to do; this says
# what a session on this machine may run without asking, and it is written to be
# read by whoever inspects the machine, not only by the harness. `bin/runnables
# compile kiosk-1` turns it into the settings the sessions read; nobody edits
# that output by hand, and no session writes it.
#
# ADMISSION IS A MERGE TO MAIN (Autumn, 2026-09-26, "for now"). An agent may
# propose a line here, or narrow one. A widening lands only by a merged PR. The
# signed control branch and its passkey gesture replace the merge later.
#
# PROOF COMES FIRST. An `allow` reaches the settings only for a holder whose
# blob at this checkout's HEAD is listed in bay/runnables.proven. An unproven
# allow is left off, so the harness treats it as it would with no list at all,
# and the compiler says which. That is how the bay says a
# tool of our own deserves the list: the same question it asks of a payload
# from outside, answered for our own bytes.
#
# Lines:
#
#   checkout <path>                   where the admitted code runs, relative to
#                                     the directory sessions start in (~/code)
#   runner <run> <tool> [prefix...]   how a claim of that `run` is started, as
#                                     the harness sees it. The FIRST line per run
#                                     is the canonical form, the only one an
#                                     allow is written for; every form gets the
#                                     denies, so a secret has no side door
#   narrow <answer> <holder> | <shape>
#                                     answer this verb more tightly than its
#                                     class does. Only ever tighter: a `narrow`
#                                     that loosens is refused by the compiler

checkout  work/fcpublicmedia.org@media-node

# UNCONFIRMED: the media node's venv path. Placeholder until kiosk answers.
runner  python      Bash        python
runner  sh          Bash
runner  powershell  Bash        powershell -NoProfile -File
runner  powershell  PowerShell  &

# The checkout is the live one: a file written into it leaves it dirty, and the
# door's rebase skips a dirty worktree, so the screens stop updating (the same
# reason `gotcha` commits). Building belongs in a work/ branch here, so on this
# machine it asks.
narrow  ask   bin/build-kiosk.py | -

# Launching the screens and reviving sessions already ask, by class. They are
# the operator's and the attendant's to do once those roles exist; a dev session
# should not need them at all.
